An explicit range makes a parenthesized binder unambiguous even when its
body starts with a unary operator. Ordinary contextual-keyword calls keep
their binary operators.

-- in.cue --
x: forall (n in 1 | 2) >=n
y: exists (n in 1 | 2) -n
z: forall (b in true | false) !b
ordinary: forall(x) + 1
-- debug.txt --
x: forall (n in 1|2) >=n
